<title>GERMANY: TABLE - German April unadj numbers in work rise m-m.</title>
<headline>TABLE - German April unadj numbers in work rise m-m.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN NUMBERS IN WORK		 Apr 97   Mar 97   Apr 96</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(unadj, million)    33.898   33.830   34.389</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(seas adj, million) 34.027   34.047   34.523</p>
<p> Number in work (2)(seas adj, million) 34.065   34.083   34.568</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj,million)	  27.851   27.783   28.181</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)    27.939   27.941   28.272</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)	  6.080    6.058    6.248</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)     6.126    6.142    6.296</p>
<p>NOTE - Pan-German figure marked (1) refer to people living in Germany. Those marked (2), as well as all the west and east German figures, refer to people working in the respective regions but not necessarily living in Germany.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
